{"step_index":2274,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T10:16:46Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-27T15:46:46+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-27T15:46:46+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/scratch/test_guide_gen.py`\nTotal Lines: 75\nTotal Bytes: 4147\nShowing lines 1 to 60\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # scratch/test_guide_gen.py\n2: # Tests the rule-based educational teaching guide generator\n3: \n4: def generate_teaching_guide(p):\n5:     title = p.get('title', 'DSA Problem')\n6:     pattern = p.get('pattern', 'Algorithmic Pattern')\n7:     topic = p.get('primaryTopic', 'Data Structures')\n8:     summary = p.get('summary') or p.get('description', '')\n9:     \n10:     # Section A: Understand\n11:     what_is_asked = f\"The problem asks you to {summary.lower().rstrip('.')}. You must process the input and return the requested result meeting the specified time and space bounds.\"\n12:     \n13:     # What to return\n14:     if 'index' in summary.lower() or 'indices' in summary.lower():\n15:         what_to_return = \"Return the 0-based index or indices satisfying the target condition (e.g., [i, j]).\"\n16:     elif 'true' in summary.lower() or 'false' in summary.lower() or 'determine if' in summary.lower() or 'check if' in summary.lower():\n17:         what_to_return = \"Return a boolean value: True if the condition holds, False otherwise.\"\n18:     elif 'maximum' in summary.lower() or 'largest' in summary.lower():\n19:         what_to_return = \"Return the single maximum / optimal numeric value found.\"\n20:     elif 'minimum' in summary.lower() or 'shortest' in summary.lower():\n21:         what_to_return = \"Return the single minimum / shortest numeric value found.\"\n22:     elif 'list' in summary.lower() or 'array' in summary.lower() or 'group' in summary.lower():\n23:         what_to_return = \"Return the resulting list or array containing the c\n<truncated 593 bytes>\n elements appear at the very start or end of the collection.\"\n33:     ]\n34: \n35:     # Section B: Learn the Pattern\n36:     why_useful = f\"A naive brute-force approach typically requires checking all combinations in O(n²) or O(2^n) time. The {pattern} pattern reduces time complexity to optimal {p.get('timeComplexity', 'O(n)')} by keeping track of essential state and avoiding redundant checks.\"\n37:     \n38:     small_example = f\"For a small input with 2 or 3 elements, {pattern} tracks key invariants step by step. When the target state is matched, it terminates immediately rather than scanning remaining unnecessary paths.\"\n39:     \n40:     intended_approach = [\n41:         f\"1. Initialize state: Set up necessary variables, pointers, or data structures for the {pattern} approach.\",\n42:         \"2. Iterate and update: Traverse the input once, updating your invariants and checking for the target condition.\",\n43:         \"3. Finalize result: Return the computed answer or fallback default if no match was found.\"\n44:     ]\n45: \n46:     # Hints\n47:     hints = [\n48:         f\"Hint 1 (Observation): What redundant work can you eliminate instead of re-scanning all elements? Think about what you already know at each step.\",\n49:         f\"Hint 2 (Data Structure): How can the {pattern} pattern or an auxiliary lookup structure help you achieve {p.get('timeComplexity', 'O(n)')} time?\",\n50:         f\"Hint 3 (Algorithm): Follow the invariant: maintain current state as you iterate, and check if the complement or boundary satisfies the goal.\"\n51:     ]\n52: \n53:     return {\n54:         \"whatIsAsked\": what_is_asked,\n55:         \"whatToReturn\": what_to_return,\n56:         \"edgeCases\": edge_cases,\n57:         \"whyUseful\": why_useful,\n58:         \"smallExample\": small_example,\n59:         \"intendedApproach\": intended_approach,\n60:         \"hints\": hints\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
